Converting decimal to hexadecimal is similar to converting decimal to binary,
but instead of dividing by 2, you divide by 16.

The method: divide by 16 repeatedly, read remainders backward.

STEP-BY-STEP: Convert 42 to hex

Step	|  Division	|  Result	|  Remainder
-----------------------------------------------------
1	    |  42 ÷ 16	|  2	    |  10 (which is A in hex)
2	    |  2 ÷ 16  	|  0	    |  2

Read remainders from bottom to top: 2A

So 42 in decimal = 0x2A.

EXAMPLE 2: Convert 255 to hex

Step	|  Division	|  Result	|  Remainder
-----------------------------------------------------
1	    |  255 ÷ 16	|  15	    |  15 (which is F in hex)
2	    |  15 ÷ 16	|  0	    |  15 (F)
Read bottom to top: FF

So 255 in decimal = 0xFF.

EXAMPLE 3: Convert 1000 to hex

Step	|  Division	  |  Result	|  Remainder
-------------------------------------------------------
1	    |  1000 ÷ 16	|  62	    |  8
2	    |  62 ÷ 16	  |  3	    |  14 (which is E in hex)
3	    |  3 ÷ 16    	|  0	    |  3

Read bottom to top: 3E8

So 1000 in decimal = 0x3E8.

Remainder reminder:

Remainder (0-15)	|  Hex digit
------------------------------
0-9	              |  0-9
10	              |  A
11	              |  B
12	              |  C
13	              |  D
14	              |  E
15	              |  F
